{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1470052-e-division-in-v5","id":1470052,"title":"E Division in V5","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-12-09T10:42:37-08:00","id":1470052,"title":"E Division in V5","content":"E Division<br /> <br /> E Division, or Enigma Division, is functionally no more.<br /> <br /> The division of archons once dealt with incidents between the Camarilla and other supernatural groups. This included werewolves, mages, fae and madder things.<br /> <br /> E Division lost a champion among Camarilla leadership with the death of Jan Pieterzoon. With the defection of the Gangrel and the Brujah, and the collapse of the Tremere pyramid, E Division lost the field agents with the most experience and important resources. Founder Karl Schrekt is preoccupied with rebuilding the Tremere hierarchy.<br /> <br /> E Division stopped being a real force by 2015.<br /> <br /> But former members and contacts still exist as do bolt holes of information and resources. It is still possible to tap into this network, and these resources. And because the Camarilla never formally shut down E Division you might get away with it.<br /> <br /> \u2022 Contacts: You know how to reach out to remaining members of Enigma Division. The people you contact will believe you but they cannot react soon. It will take a session or two before you can count on reinforcements.<br /> <br /> \u2022\u2022 Librarian: You might not know how to handle this situation but you know who will. Once per session your character may reach out to the right authorities on an issue. This person will have \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 (four) dots in the subject matters the character is investigating. This expert will except a boon in return.<br /> <br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022 Q: You have access to state of the art hardware and weapons. Once per session your character may put a call into an E Division contact to get technology and weapons. This hardware is otherwise out of reach for the characters status and wealth. E Division expects the return, in good condition, of the hardware at the end of use. They will charge you for damaged and destroyed property.<br /> <br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 A Mentor: A former member of E Division serves as your \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 (four) dot Mawla. You may turn to them to gain support, resources and information.<br /> <br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Agent: You are an active agent for E Division in as much as it has never been formally shut down. You gain Status: Camarilla \u2022\u2022\u2022 (three), and once per session you may use \u2022\u2022\u2022 Q or \u2022\u2022 Librarian.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1208,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","user":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","date":". 12-09-2021, 02:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-09T10:45:19-08:00","id":1470053,"title":"","content":"This is a great Loresheet!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-10T09:32:43-08:00","id":1470147,"title":"","content":"Thanks. This is for the update to <i>Hunger from Beyond</i>, my STV book about adding cosmic horror and mythos elements to a VtM game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-14T11:43:02-08:00","id":1470456,"title":"","content":"this?<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/281780/Hunger-from-Beyond\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/images/1/281780.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/281780/Hunger-from-Beyond\" target=\"_blank\"> Hunger from Beyond (for V20) - White Wolf | Storytellers Vault </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/281780/Hunger-from-Beyond\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/281780/Hunger-from-Beyond </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Hunger from Beyond (for V20) - &ldquo;I have seen the dark universe yawningWhere the black planets roll without aim,Where they roll in their horror unheede </div> </div> </div><br /> (which sounds really awesome, any plans on updating it fully to v5?)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>they/them.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27123-littlewitchmaus","name":"littlewitchmaus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27123_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-14T12:28:29-08:00","id":1470460,"title":"","content":"Yes, that book exactly. Or it is for that book, which I am updating to V5. What is left of E-Division gets thrown at cosmic horror problems by elders who don't want to interrupt their soiree at a nightclub or their midnight golf game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1208,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","user":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","date":". 12-14-2021, 03:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-14T14:16:44-08:00","id":1470473,"title":"","content":"I have to say I have never liked the name &quot;E Division&quot; or the idea that there are &quot;special branches&quot; of the Archons. Their numbers are just so low that there shouldn't be that level of bureaucracy. They are perfectly fine as concepts for individual archon characters, and lots more can be added to those than the ones provided in Archons &amp; Templars or elsewhere (one thing I imagine are specialists involved in repairing Masquerade breaches, ones dealing with important national governments, and some responsible for monitoring the spaces inbetween urban domains for suspicious activities like Sabbat nomad packs, vampire hunters, or Lupine warbands). But when such language makes players think there's anything like an actual organization, it ends up distorting the setting by bloating things.<br /> <br /> Having some archons specialize in certain tasks make sense, but given that each Justicar has essentially the same authority as the others, and that who occupies those roles can change, such designations don't make sense. It's like saying the &quot;Wolf Pack&quot; is a special branch of the Camarilla when it's just the personal coterie of one archon who was given some tasks to do (probably by the Gangrel Justicar Xavier). Having some vampires who specialize in enigmatic phenomenon is OK. But how many of them really were there? 3-5? That's what I imagine them to be - a very small coterie sharing information with one another perhaps with Karl Schrekt as a coordinator, and occasionally operating under the jurisdiction of their Justicar with whatever support that one personally gives them.<br /> <br /> I know that terms like &quot;Alastors&quot; and &quot;E Division&quot; are actually just nicknames, and don't really represent anything like a &quot;special branch.&quot; It's just three guys giving themselves a funny nickname. Or the Justicars bestowing a special title or project name to indicate the importance of the job being done. Those are solid concepts for STs to use in their games. But I think it's easy to forget that in the end, these are just nicknames given to some archons carrying out a specific task as opposed to some kind of organization or bureaucracy that implies large numbers.<br /> <br /> Having said that, I do like including elements of cosmic horror and paranormal mystery in my games, so I do encourage products like this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-14T18:58:31-08:00","id":1470492,"title":"","content":"My take on E Division is they were something for the PCs to be a part of, not someone they turned to in the event of a crisis. It gave some energy to a cross over game where the PCs are supposed to make the problem go away. E Division was never just something to make problems go away for the PCs and they were never there to solve problems for the PCs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-16T06:49:00-08:00","id":1470622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1470052-e-division-in-v5?p=1470473#post1470473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have to say I have never liked the name &quot;E Division&quot; or the idea that there are &quot;special branches&quot; of the Archons. Their numbers are just so low that there shouldn't be that level of bureaucracy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Archons and Templars suggest that at any given time there are around 50-250 Archons. If you assume there are members of each special-branch/division then you have:<br /> - Alastors<br /> - Dog Catchers<br /> - Dopplegangers<br /> - E-Division<br /> - Josians<br /> - Quaesitors<br /> <br /> Assuming maximum Archons that's 250 Archons across 6 divisions, say 7 for unspecialised Archons (in theory one branch per Justicar). That's 35 members per special branch/division if distributed evenly. (We know even distribution is unlikely, Josians and Doppelgangers are unlikely to be numerous; whilst there's probably above average number of Alastors as their rank can't be revoked.)<br /> <br /> (This doesn't count The Eyes, but they're the Inner Circles own troops so I don't think they count.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Having some archons specialize in certain tasks make sense, but given that each Justicar has essentially the same authority as the others, and that who occupies those roles can change, such designations don't make sense. </div> </div> </div>That assumes a new Justicar would just tear up what their predecessor has created. Unlikely for the Ventrue (Lucinde being Justicar for Unlife) and the Tremere given the relations between Shreckt and Carfax. For the Josians and the Alastors a change in Justicar doesn't really mean much. Josians are too few in number to effectively replace, their knowledge being so esoteric and rare. Meanwhile, Alastors serve for unlife and have their own formal organisation, a Justicar would need significant support (and be overturning a lot of tradition) to make major changes.<br /> <br /> Just like in modern democracies, there are still specialist forces and units. Just because leaders change doesn't mean they'll tear up the entirety of the support structure that supports their newfound position.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I know that terms like &quot;Alastors&quot; and &quot;E Division&quot; are actually just nicknames, and don't really represent anything like a &quot;special branch.&quot; It's just three guys giving themselves a funny nickname. </div> </div> </div>Really depends on the Special Branch/Division in question. In the case of Alastors they have a very formal organisation, including regional commanders and organisers other than the Justicars. They formally handle training, recruitment, targets, bringing enemies to justice, etc. Meanwhile, the Josians are more like you describe. A small band of like-minds with a useful skill set that adopted a common moniker for sake of simplicity.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I have to say I have never liked the name &quot;E Division&quot; or the idea that there are &quot;special branches&quot; of the Archons. Their numbers are just so low that there shouldn't be that level of bureaucracy. </div> </div> </div>Personally, I like the idea of some variation. Some groups of Archons have more formal organisation befitting their work, with support staff, sub-agents (Alastors, Dog Catchers); others have informal networks of peers, that share common skills and knowledge (Josians, Dopplegangers).<br /> <br /> That said, I really don't see why members of an elite conspiracy like the Camarilla, who have the wisdom of centuries wouldn't set up formal systems where they'd be useful. Especially after essentially going to war with intelligence agencies, I'd be really surprised if the Camarilla didn't formalise Archons and the divisions and start to organise them more effectively.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STV Author - <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/374164/Guide-to-the-Sabbat?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=0_0_45624_0_0_0_0\" target=\"_blank\">Guide to the Sabbat</a> <br /> Current Project(s): Tales from the Fronts - A Guide to the Gehenna War","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25061-karos","name":"Karos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25061_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-16T07:24:39-08:00","id":1470625,"title":"","content":"Another thing to consider is the possibility of overlap. There's no reason for a single individual to pertain to more than one &quot;division&quot;. It is a division of resources and work, not necessarily personnel. Especially considering that in practical terms they're not necessarily being called for duty at any of them too frequently, as even in their specialties most problems will be dealt with locally.<br /> <br /> One other possibility, related to this, is for the existence of guides and structures more than divisions, but that may need some tweak. In this angle things like the E Division don't have members all the time, but at any moment that someone needs to do the job, they can be granted access to the resources of the Division and the guidelines set for the task. It may even have special identities with contacts and resources attached to them, but to be assumed by authorized personnel. <br /> <br /> Finally, while certainly not the focus of the descriptions, those divisions may also work a lot through Ghouls and mortal agents. A single vampire may supervise an entire active Division and its assets, and recruit other vampires when needed for a task.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}